  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1217 PM CDT Sun May 31 2026\n\nMonday looks to be the hottest day of the forecast period, with\nafternoon highs reaching the low to mid 90s. Heat index values\nwill again top out over 100 degrees in some places. A weak\nbackdoor cool front will push across the area Monday night and\nTuesday, and may result in an isolated storm or two in a few spots\nmainly Monday evening and overnight. Temperatures and dew points\nwill both lower slightly Tuesday, with even cooler and drier air\nmoving in by Wednesday. \n\nAn upper level storm system will approach from the west by the end\nof the week into next weekend bringing a return to daily shower\nand thunderstorm chances. Temperatures through this period will\nremain near the seasonal averages for early June.",
